# Contract over invention

If `docs/lld.md`, `docs/backend-structure.md`, or the current task does not state the behavior, stop and name the missing line. Do not pick a plausible field, status, message, index, or package.

Confirm an unfamiliar Express, Mongoose, Zod, Vitest, argon2, jsonwebtoken, or pino signature with the Context7 MCP before writing the call.

## Allowed results

`DomainError` codes: `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `INVALID_CREDENTIALS`, `UNAUTHENTICATED`, `FORBIDDEN`, `DOCTOR_NOT_FOUND`, `PATIENT_NOT_FOUND`, `EMAIL_IN_USE`, `RATE_LIMITED`, `INTERNAL`.

HTTP statuses: `200`, `201`, `400`, `401`, `403`, `404`, `409`, `429`, `500`. Health uses `503` only when the database ping fails. Delete and logout are `200`, not `204`. `INTERNAL` from `DomainError` stays `500`.

Success `message` text comes from the task or the LLD.

## Filler that does not ship

- `any`, `as any`, `as unknown as`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error`, `eslint-disable`
- `TODO`, `FIXME`, `not implemented`, `lorem ipsum`, `coming soon`
- An empty `catch`, a swallowed error, or a default return that hides a missing rule
- A new layer, helper, or endpoint the task did not name
- Comments that restate the next line. A comment is only for a constraint the code cannot show.

```typescript
// Bad: guessed code and a type escape
throw new DomainError("NOT_FOUND" as any);

// Good: the code the LLD names
throw new DomainError("DOCTOR_NOT_FOUND");
```
